From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: lgm-sso: zero-initialize struct led_init_data

sso_create_led() declares struct led_init_data on the stack and only
fills in fwnode, devicename and default_label, leaving devname_mandatory
(and any other future field) as uninitialized stack garbage. That's
flagged by UBSAN at every LED registration:

  UBSAN: invalid-load in drivers/leds/led-class.c:494:16
  load of value 16 is not a valid value for type '_Bool'

Zero-initialize the struct so all bool/numeric fields default to 0/false.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -349,7 +349,7 @@ static int sso_create_led(struct sso_led
 			  struct fwnode_handle *child)
 {
 	struct sso_led_desc *desc = &led->desc;
-	struct led_init_data init_data;
+	struct led_init_data init_data = {};
 	int err;
 
 	init_data.fwnode = child;
